# System Integration First

- For bug fixes and feature changes, implement the behavior in the core system flow, not as surface-level workarounds.
- Avoid one-off "patch-only" logic that bypasses the main pipeline unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer shared, reusable logic paths that naturally cover all relevant shapes/cases.
- If a quick fix is added temporarily, replace it with a robust integrated solution in the same task whenever feasible.
- Keep user-visible behavior stable while improving internals.

## Preferred approach

1. Identify the canonical pipeline for the behavior.
2. Integrate the fix there so all callers benefit.
3. Remove or reduce legacy heuristics that conflict with the canonical logic.
4. Verify no regressions in related interactions (selection, visuals, drag, merge/split states).
